
@startuml
!define RECTANGLE class

start
:Check Prerequisites;
note right
  - Public GitHub repository
  - Existing custom component
  - Home Assistant compatibility
end note

:Assess Current Repository Structure;

if (Repository structure compliant?) then (no)
  :Reorganize Files;
  :Create custom_components/{domain} directory;
  :Move integration files to proper location;
else (yes)
  :Continue with current structure;
endif

:Create/Update hacs.json;
note right
  - Set display name
  - Define minimum HA version
  - Configure content settings
  - Set render_readme option
end note

:Update manifest.json;
note right
  - Add version field
  - Include documentation URL
  - Add issue tracker URL
  - Set codeowners
end note

:Create GitHub Actions Workflows;
split
  :Setup HACS Validation;
  note right
    - Validate HACS compliance
    - Check repository structure
  end note
split again
  :Setup Hassfest Validation;
  note right
    - Validate Home Assistant standards
    - Check manifest compliance
  end note
end split

:Create/Update Documentation;
split
  :Update README.md;
split again
  :Create info.md (optional);
  note right
    Rich content for HACS UI
  end note
split again
  :Add installation instructions;
end split

:Test Integration Locally;

if (Local testing successful?) then (no)
  :Debug and Fix Issues;
  :Retry Local Testing;
else (yes)
  :Continue;
endif

:Create GitHub Release;
note right
  - Tag version
  - Include release notes
  - Provide installation assets
end note

:Test via HACS Custom Repository;

if (HACS testing successful?) then (no)
  :Fix HACS compatibility issues;
  :Update configuration files;
  :Create new release;
else (yes)
  :Continue;
endif

:Submit for HACS Default Repository;
note right
  - Follow HACS submission guidelines
  - Provide integration details
  - Wait for community review
end note

:Integration Available in HACS;

stop
@enduml
